    "updated_at": "2022-04-06T18:32:25Z",
    "body": "LGTM. Is it worth including a Firefox Android example here because its navigator.appVersion, unlike Firefox desktop, includes a space and a version number like \"<code data-x=\"\">5.0 (Android 11)</code>\"?\r\n\r\nMDN's `navigator.appVersion` documentation is also out of date:\r\n\r\n> Returns either \"4.0\" or a string representing version information about the browser. \r\n\r\nhttps://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Navigator/appVersion",
